module param_mode.pos_1

// A parameter MODE, and the effect is VISIBLE: the program prints 42, byte for
// byte with the oracle. `mut v int` is what std writes 131 times.
//
// novac REFUSED this file until 2026-08-21, and the refusal wore a lie for a
// face: "novac does not know this type yet", pointing at `int`. Both collectors
// read a parameter's type by the fixed index `pk[1]`, which is the MODE's slot
// when a mode is written -- so the NAME was read as the type. The typing walk
// had been moved onto the `param_name_at`/`param_type_at` doors on 2026-08-18;
// the collectors were not, and nothing noticed because nothing in the corpus
// declares a mode.
//
// The same fixed index in the DECLARATION path was worse than a wrong message:
// it dropped the whole signature, so every `consume` method of std -- both
// finalize-lane `#coerce` pairs among them -- was invisible to novac.
fn bump(mut v int) -> int => v + 1

fn main() {
    ro x = 41
    println(bump(x))
}
